# Cursor Performance (Agent + Operator)

Cursor lag in this repo is almost always **watcher/index noise** + **CPU-heavy
scripts running in parallel**, not git history size. Follow these rules on every
session.

> **절대 금지 정본:** [`80-absolute-gate-prohibitions.mdc`](80-absolute-gate-prohibitions.mdc) (G1·G2·G4)

## Agent terminal discipline (mandatory)

See **`78-cursor-auto-hygiene.mdc`** — `.cursor/hooks.json` + `pretest`/`posttest`
가 세션·shell·테스트 전후 정리를 **자동** 실행. 아래는 hook 실패 시 에이전트
fallback.

- **One heavy gate at a time.** Never run `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, `build`,
  or `check` in parallel across multiple terminals or background shells.
- **Use incremental checks during work:**
  - `bun run typecheck` (~2s) — default
  - `bun run typecheck:force` — only after tsconfig/project-reference changes or
    suspicious stale diagnostics
  - `bun run lint` — uses ESLint cache automatically
- **Never run full `bun run check` for a narrow change.** Pick the smallest gate:
  `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, or a targeted Playwright spec.
- **After E2E or coverage:** `bun run clean` runs automatically via post-hooks;
  still verify with `git status` that `test-results/` and `playwright-report/`
  are gone.
- **After local `build` when the session ends:** run `bun run clean` manually
  (post-build auto-clean would delete dist immediately — do not add that).
- **Never** start E2E in a background shell. See `77-e2e-lifecycle.mdc`.
- **Do not leave diagnostic shells running** (`Get-Process`, hung `tasklist`,
  full-repo file counts). They compete with TypeScript/ESLint and freeze the UI.
- **Low-spec operator PC:** see **`79-low-spec-pc.mdc`** — vitest/playwright single-worker,
  one terminal / one heavy gate, no background shells, `check:full` only after E2E stable.
- **Lag spike:** `bun run cursor:status` then `bun run cursor:emergency-reset` before any new gate.

## MCP and Cursor runtime

- Project `.cursor/mcp.json` stays minimal. Do not add duplicate Supabase MCP
  servers (plugin + stdio races on Windows).
- After clone or MCP errors: `bun run mcp:fix`, then **fully quit and reopen
  Cursor** (tray icon too).
- Do not enable heavy global MCP servers unless required for the task.

## Generated output contract

When adding **generated** or **high-volume** paths (build output, caches, SQL
mirrors, large dumps):

1. `.gitignore`
2. `.cursorignore`
3. `scripts/lib/workspace-artifacts.ts` (single source of truth)
4. `scripts/clean-artifacts.ts` imports from workspace-artifacts (sync enforced
   by `check:hygiene`)
5. `.vscode/settings.json` → `files.watcherExclude` + `search.exclude`

**Never** leave a new artifact directory without all five updates.

## Operator habits (Windows)

- **Restart Cursor** after `.cursorignore` or `.vscode/settings.json` changes.
- **Stop Docker Desktop** when not running local Supabase — it adds constant CPU
  and file watcher load.
- **Defender exclusion** (optional): add repo `node_modules` to Windows Defender
  exclusions if scans coincide with lag spikes. On this PC V3 Lite is often the
  active AV — run `bun run cursor:av-exclusions` (opens V3 Lite + prints paths).
- **Session start preflight:** `bun run cursor:preflight` (clean + config check).
  **자동:** `sessionStart` hook → `cursor:session-start` (`.cursor/hooks.json`).
- **Monthly metadata sweep:** `bun run cursor:clean-metadata` (dry-run preview).
  Apply with `bun run cursor:clean-metadata -- --apply`. Old AI transcripts and
  terminal logs live **outside the git repo** under
  `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\projects\…` — safe to delete; `@` past-chat links in
  Cursor may break for those sessions.

## Outside-repo Cursor data (not indexed by phonara-gb)

| Location | Typical size | Safe to clean? | Impact on lag |
|----------|--------------|----------------|---------------|
| `~\.cursor\projects\…\agent-transcripts` | small–large | Yes (`cursor:clean-metadata`) | Low unless huge |
| `~\.cursor\projects\…\terminals` | small | Yes | Low |
| `%APPDATA%\Cursor\logs` | ~86MB+ | Yes (`--include-cursor-logs`) | Medium |
| `%APPDATA%\Cursor\User` | ~2GB+ | **No** (settings, state) | Main disk use, not workspace index |
| `%APPDATA%\Cursor\snapshots` | ~264MB+ | Manual only | Occasional |
| `~\.cursor\ai-tracking` | ~37MB | Optional (`--include-cursor-logs`) | Low |

Repo `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/mcp.json` are **source of truth — never delete**.

## Quality gate

`bun run check:hygiene` is part of `bun run check` and CI. It fails when:

- Required watcher/index patterns are missing from config files
- `clean-artifacts` drifts from `workspace-artifacts.ts`
- Session residue (`test-results/`, `playwright-report/`, `coverage/`, E2E auth
  tokens) is still on disk
